15:["$","div",null,{"className":"article-layout","children":[["$","aside",null,{"className":"article-aside","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"IN THIS STORY"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"#definition","children":["01 / ","The essential"]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"#analysis","children":["02 / ","The analysis"]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"#practice","children":["03 / ","In practice"]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"#sources","children":["04 / ","Sources & limits"]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/en/lexicon/","children":["↗ ","The AGD lexicon"]}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"article-text","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"quick-answer","id":"definition","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"THE TAKEAWAY"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"AI Slop describes output that puts volume ahead of distinctiveness and usefulness. It is an editorial judgment about the result, not an automatic diagnosis based on which tool made it."}]]}],["$","$L18",null,{"a":"$1:props:children:1:props:article","lang":"en"}],"$undefined",["$","section",null,{"id":"analysis","className":"article-prose","children":[["$","p","0",{"children":"Sometimes you recognize the brief before you understand the video. Two seconds of surprise, a voice that never doubts, three benefits, an imaginary button. The issue is not that a machine speaks. It is that nobody seems to have anything to say."}],["$","p","1",{"children":"AI can widen the creative field: prototype a setting, try a narrative, visualize something impossible to film. It can also compress twenty perspectives into one perfectly forgettable average. Output speed cannot distinguish those uses."}],["$","p","2",{"children":"In an AGD network, diversity should survive the removal of account names. Mix nine posts from three personas and ask someone to reconstruct the groups. If the only difference is subtitle color, you have probably distributed a template rather than identities."}],["$","p","3",{"children":"Before adding variants, change a fundamental choice: the conflict, the intended audience or the knowledge offered. An idea worth a human version may deserve a synthetic version too. The reverse does not become true because a subscription includes a thousand generations."}]]}],["$","blockquote",null,{"children":["“","Your generator doesn’t need a better prompt. Your account needs a point of view.","”"]}],"$undefined",false,["$","$L18",null,{"a":"$1:props:children:1:props:article","lang":"en","number":2}],["$","section",null,{"id":"practice","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Put it to work."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"checklist","children":[["$","li","0",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":["0",1]}],"Mix nine posts and test whether personas remain recognizable."]}],["$","li","1",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":["0",2]}],"Change the perspective before the rendering."]}],["$","li","2",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":["0",3]}],"Delete passages that communicate nothing."]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"sources","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"What this does not prove."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"caveat","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The limit. "}],"High output does not demonstrate creative diversity or audience satisfaction."]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sources","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"SOURCES & PROVENANCE"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Original analysis of the AGD framework provided by TokPortal, lexicon and doctrine (2026). Examples are illustrative. No proprietary study or customer outcome is claimed."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"editorial-note","children":["FEEDRAID is an editorial project initiated by TokPortal. That relationship is separate from the evidence behind claims. AI-assisted writing; no fictional journalist identities."," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/en/about/","children":"Our editorial policy →"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"next-read","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"THE CURRENT CONTINUES"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/en/read/doctrine/account-isolation/","children":"50 accounts. One idea. Zero strategy."}]}],"$L19"]}]]}],"$L1a"]}]
16:["$","section",null,{"className":"related-grid","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":["$","h2",null,{"children":"Other currents."}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article-grid","children":[["$","$L1b","017",{"a":{"id":"017","slug":"hook-slop","term":"Hook Slop","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"hook-slop","tier":"editorial","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["faceless-account","account-persona","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"“Stop scrolling”: everybody is shouting the same thing.","dek":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value.","point":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value. It is an editorial criticism, not a platform category.","body":["A good opening makes a promise the rest fulfills. “I lost my notes before the exam” creates a specific situation. “This app will change your life” could sell anything. Compare the first sentence with the conclusion: if they address different problems, early retention may measure delayed disappointment.","Try rewriting without commands or spectacular adjectives. Replace the demand to stay with the situation you will resolve. If the opening becomes clearer, precision has improved. Then evaluate the full piece: a quieter hook may attract fewer curious viewers and more people facing the actual problem. That possibility is worth testing, not asserting as a universal advantage of restrained creative work."],"action":["Connect the opening to visible evidence.","Remove superlatives that add nothing."],"trap":"Better opening retention does not guarantee that the promise is delivered later.","quote":"“Stop scrolling”: everybody is shouting the same thing.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"“Stop scrolling”: everybody is shouting the same thing.","text":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Hook Slop","text":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value. It is an editorial criticism, not a platform category.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Better opening retention does not guarantee that the promise is delivered later.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Connect the opening to visible evidence.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Remove superlatives that add nothing.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg","width":1280,"height":1707,"alt":{"en":"A red and cream handheld megaphone with a coiled microphone cord."},"credit":"Solomon203","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 20e7e1574fe6745909375e5658e0229e84fcafe0.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seikaku_ER-56_20190217.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}],["$","$L1b","007",{"a":{"id":"007","slug":"content-isolation","term":"Content Isolation","category":"doctrine","kind":"essay","image":"content-isolation","tier":"canonical","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["content-saturation","multi-account-strategy","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"New subtitles do not make a new idea.","dek":"Content Isolation preserves meaningful creative differences between accounts: narrative, angle, format or purpose.","point":"Content Isolation preserves meaningful creative differences between accounts: narrative, angle, format or purpose. It complements Account Isolation, which differentiates distribution surfaces.","body":["One problem can become a precise demo, a failure story or a comparison of habits. Those versions offer different information. Recoloring an edit preserves its structure and perspective. Archive concepts with their variations so you know whether you are testing an idea or its packaging.","Take an exam-preparation video. One version explains scheduling, another tells a story about forgetting, and a third compares revision methods. They share raw material but change the question addressed. Record that question in the brief. It becomes a practical reason to reject a supposedly new version that merely changes its colors while preserving the same argument and viewing experience."],"action":["Assign an identifier to each creative concept.","Record what each version changes for the viewer."],"trap":"Duplication can make one looping idea look like many experiments.","quote":"New subtitles do not make a new idea.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"New subtitles do not make a new idea.","text":"Content Isolation preserves meaningful creative differences between accounts: narrative, angle, format or purpose.","media":"/images/editorial/content-isolation.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Content Isolation","text":"Content Isolation preserves meaningful creative differences between accounts: narrative, angle, format or purpose. It complements Account Isolation, which differentiates distribution surfaces.","media":"/images/editorial/content-isolation.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Duplication can make one looping idea look like many experiments.","media":"/images/editorial/content-isolation.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Assign an identifier to each creative concept.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/content-isolation.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Record what each version changes for the viewer.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/content-isolation.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/content-isolation.jpg","width":1280,"height":1707,"alt":{"en":"Individual letterpress printing blocks sorted into compartments of a wooden tray."},"credit":"Ross Dunn","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: e81a9124f021a76db25f5651107674c2b318b15f.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Printing_Press_letters_for_long_gone,_traditional_newsprint_(41343604484).jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}],"$L1c"]}]]}]
