1c:["$","$L1b","016",{"a":{"id":"016","slug":"account-persona","term":"Account Persona","category":"creative","kind":"essay","image":"account-persona","tier":"canonical","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["hook-slop","creative-matrix","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A persona is not a photo and a name.","dek":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return..","point":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return.","body":["Write the opinions this account can defend and the topics it leaves to others. A rushed student does not discuss an app like an organizational consultant. Character appears through chosen details, not a biography full of adjectives. A fictional persona should be identifiable as such when it could be mistaken for a real person.","Test the character against a frustration. What happens when the app does not solve everything? A credible voice can acknowledge a limit, propose a manual workaround or reject an unsuitable use. If the persona only praises the product, its identity may collapse when the audience asks an unexpected question. A consistent boundary often reveals more character than another carefully chosen visual accessory."],"action":["Write three opinions and three refusals.","Test consistency across five scripts."],"trap":"An invented testimonial does not become acceptable because a persona delivers it.","quote":"A persona is not a photo and a name.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A persona is not a photo and a name.","text":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return..","media":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Account Persona","text":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return.","media":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"An invented testimonial does not become acceptable because a persona delivers it.","media":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Write three opinions and three refusals.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Test consistency across five scripts.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg","width":1280,"height":875,"alt":{"en":"Carved stone theatrical masks displayed among the ruins of Ostia Antica."},"credit":"Dennis G. Jarvis","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 5a244f48cf59ebe7c71fe44087df41410beb2633.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italy_-_Ostia_Antica_-_Theatre_Masks_(5149585364).jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
